{title: 326 - Open My Eyes That I May See}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #326 • OPEN MY EYES THAT I MAY  • 16.17.16.12}
{lyricist: Clara H. Scott}
{composer: Clara H. Scott}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 326}
{meta: tune OPEN MY EYES THAT I MAY }
{meta: meter 16.17.16.12}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Fm/C]Open [Cm]my eyes, that I [Db]may see Glimpses [Cm/G]of truth [Eb/G]Thou hast for me;
[Eb/G]Place in my hands the [Ab]wonderful key That [Bbm]shall unclasp [Db/Ab]and set me free.
[Db/Ab]Silently [Ab]now I wait [Fm]for Thee, Ready, [Bbm/F]my [Eb/Bb]God, Thy will to see;
[Cm/G]Open my eyes, illumine me, Spirit Divine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Fm/C]Open [Cm]my [Db]ears that [Cm/G]I [Eb/G]may hear
[Fm/C]Voices [Cm]of [Db]truth Thou [Cm/G]sendest [Eb]clear;
[Eb/G]and while the [Ab]wavenotes [Bbm]fall [Db/Ab]on my ear,
[Db/Ab]Everything [Fm]false [Bbm/F]will [Eb/Bb]disappear.
[Db/Ab]Silently [Fm]now I [Bbm/F]wait [Eb/Bb]for Thee,
[Db/Ab]Ready, [Ab]my [Fm]God, Thy [Bbm/F]will [Eb/Bb]to see;
[Cm/G]Open my ears, illumine me, Spirit Divine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Fm/C]Open [Cm]my [Db]mouth, and [Cm/G]let [Eb/G]me bear
[Fm/C]Gladly [Cm]the warm [Db]truth [Cm/G]everywhere;
[Eb/G]Open my [Ab]heart, and [Bbm]let me [Db/Ab]prepare
[Db/Ab]Love with [Ab]Thy [Fm]children [Bbm/F]thus [Eb/Bb]to share.
[Db/Ab]Silently [Fm]now I [Bbm/F]wait [Eb/Bb]for Thee,
[Db/Ab]Ready, [Ab]my [Fm]God, Thy [Bbm/F]will [Eb/Bb]to see;
[Cm/G]Open my heart, illumine me, Spirit Divine!
{end_of_verse}
